      "disposition": "applied",
      "reason": "The native builder applies interface ablation and carrier migration to the declared P1-to-P2 Relay link. It changes only transport to available paper, preserves both parent functions and all four initial jobs, and constructs original-link, transferred-link, broken-link, co-presence and separate parent-alone conditions. It explicitly admits that parent-only band computation defeats an interaction claim based on correctness alone. The supported rejoin probe and burden accounting survive the handoff. Application is established by the actual role texts; experimental outcomes remain unknown.",
      "handoff_fidelity": true,
      "source_support": true,
      "resource_fit": true,
      "separating_probe_or_refusal": "Compare same-record P1/P2 provenance with M1/M2 across the two carriers and the isolated, co-present and parent-alone conditions. For later adaptation, complete mute at 12, retain the permissive latch, rejoin 12-13, and complete the isolated-transport ping at 13.5; snapshot 13.5-14. Recurrence predicts a new ping-triggered Q at 13.5, due 17.5; Escape predicts none. M3 distinguishes this from earlier queued Q, while M4 establishes controls and attempted-write permission without exposing payload or emitter effect. Direct preset inspection and an emitter sensor are explicitly unavailable. At most three earlier selected send triggers precede the ping, so the eight-Q cap cannot censor this discriminator.",
      "burden": "The serialized proposal completes I1-I4 by t=9: eight initial parent minutes plus two paper transfers totaling one minute. Fixtures cost 8.5 actor-minutes, including the final paper transfer; isolation/restoration, mute, rejoin, ping and two snapshots total four. Q service costs zero because it is optional. Total actor labor is 21.5 minutes, with 0.5 idle, finishing at 22 within the 40-minute horizon. The one actor and printer are never double-booked; planned buffered records fit the four-record capacity. The builder retains a conservative six-trigger ceiling. Stage1 K6 states five; native stage2 S6 explicitly corrects it to six, and the builder carries that correction. This is a bounded count discrepancy in the earlier role, not evidence of non-application.",
