      "source_support": true,
      "resource_fit": true,
      "separating_probe_or_refusal": "Following mute 2.5-3, perform the sole retained-preset rejoin 12-13 under the initially permissive latch, then the sole ping 13-13.5 and snapshot 13.5-14. M4 must establish completed controls and a permitted attempted write; M3 must identify a new Q triggered by this ping rather than the old pending inquiry. Escape predicts zero new Q and cumulative Q=1; Recurrence predicts one new Q at 13.5, due 17.5, and cumulative Q=2. Seven slots remain before the ping. Denied writes, mute-only silence and burden/ticket totals cannot separate these accounts.",
      "burden": "Initial parents cost eight actor-minutes. Mute 0.5, rejoin 1, ping 0.5 and snapshot 0.5 add 2.5, totaling 10.5 actor-minutes. Fixtures and Q service cost zero. Four 0.5-minute Relay transits consume no actor time; all initial tickets finish at 10.5. The actor idles to the legal rejoin start at 12; the snapshot finishes at 14, with 3.5 cumulative idle minutes. Buffer occupancy is at most one. The proposed passive continuation to 40 adds no scheduled actor action; no later complete snapshot is allocated. The proposal does not claim observed follow-through.",
